From 3088a72182142449d78067a67a98e47cd8ddc248 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 07:47:05 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] Refusal the earlier history caused: compact once and
 retry the same message

Chat 20261102_175427_594451: three harmless questions in a row were refused by
Anthropic's filter. The refusal came on the turn's first call with no tool
round, so the request differed from the last answered one only by a benign
message: the earlier history was the trigger. Recovery dropped the refused
turn and resent that same history, and the notice said "you're not stuck,
just ask something else", so every re-ask was refused again.

handle_content_policy_refusal (after the configured fallback try) now asks
agent/turn_refusal_history.history_refusal_step: when the refused request is
earlier history + only this turn's user row, it force-compacts the earlier
history once (trigger=content_policy_history, head/tail protection minimized,
the current message as verbatim tail), arms restart_with_compressed_messages
and resends the same message. A summary that does not commit, or a refused
retry (one per turn), closes the turn with copy that names the history and
points at /new. Refusals after a tool round, a first message, or a
compaction that cannot run keep the drop-and-notice path. Log line:
"history-triggered refusal: compacted+retried outcome=<retried|refused|summary_refused|compaction_skipped>".
